  "node_id": "lemma_10",
  "edition": "Newton, Principia, Andrew Motte trans., 1729 (Wikisource); Book I, Section I, Lemma X; Plate 2.",
  "caption": "The spaces which a body describes from rest under any finite force are, from the very beginning of the motion, in the duplicate ratio of the times.",
  "n_steps": 2,
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "gloss": "The same figure as Lemma IX, now read as physics: the baseline is TIME, the ordinates are VELOCITY, and the curve is the growth of speed under a force."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "gloss": "By Lemma IX the two triangular areas are the spaces described, and since they stand in the duplicate ratio of the times we obtain s proportional to t squared, whence Cor. 4 gives force proportional to space over time squared."
    }
  ],
